i'll echo what mordae said:

- keep the cursed gain level - it's useful to get out of
  the sanctum easier
- cursed scrolls of teleportation are nice for:
  - going from rodney down to VS level
  - going from VS level down to sanctum (and hopefully land on the
left
    side of the level. i just had a nasty time in the sanctum
yesterday
    with a particularly bad summoning storm. You don't want to deal
    with that crowd of monsters if you don't have to)
- means of finding traps on the planes.
  - cursed ?gold detection for any plane except fire
  - confused ?gold detection if you have a good way of confusing
    yourself (remember that casting a spell you have forgotten
    can stun you as well)
  - crystal ball - it puts you in a trance for several turns so
    you have to be careful where you use it
  - and of course the usuals. the bell, /oSDD, cast detect unseen, etc
  - i prefer cursed ?gd on all levels except fire where i use
confused ?gd
- ring of conflict. i put it on as soon as i start the ascension run,
  but some others only use it on astral. It just makes things so much
  easier.
- why is your magicbane only +2? i prefer +7. <start flamewar>. not
the
  end of the world as you shouldn't be meleeing very much.
- why are your daggers only +4? you'll generally want to avoid casting
  once you're holding the amulet. not the end of the world.
- only 1 wand of death is usually enough, but i like to have more
  just in case
- wand of slow monster for air elementals on plane of air
- keep the ring of free action on as much as you can. paralysis is one
of
  the few remaining instadeaths you are vulnerable to at this point
- i'm assuming with your sack you have a holy water or remove curse
item
  in it just in case your BoH gets cursed.
- i always use boots of jumping on astral, but you can use the spell
as
  well. You can jump through doors at an angle and teleport everybody
out
  of your way to do it. Except the riders, when you teleport them they
  teleport right next to you. But jumping makes astral much easier
  (as i learned from sjdevnull, etc)



